\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark! The song of holy voices, 
\par Chanting at the crystal sea:
\par Hallelujah! Hallelujah!
\par Hallelujah! Lord, to Thee:
\par Multitude, which none can number,
\par Like the stars in glory stand,
\par Clothed in white apparel, holding
\par Palms of victory in their hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. They have come from tribulation,
\par And have washed their robes in blood,
\par Washed them in the blood of Jesus;
\par Tried they were, and firm they stood;
\par Mocked, imprisoned, stoned, tormented,
\par Sawn asunder, slain with sword,
\par They have conquered death and Satan
\par By the might of Christ the Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Marching with Thy Cross their banner,
\par They have triumphed, following
\par Thee, the Captain of salvation,
\par Thee, their Saviour and their King.
\par Gladly, Lord, with Thee they suffered;
\par Gladly, Lord, with Thee they died;
\par And, by death, to life immortal
\par They were born and glorified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. God of God, the One-begotten,
\par Light of Light, Immanuel,
\par In whose body joined together
\par All the saints for ever dwell,
\par Pour upon us of Thy fullness,
\par That we may for evermore
\par God the Father, God the Son, and 
\par God the Holy Ghost adore.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

